# HTTP examples for module 15-observability. Run them from IntelliJ IDEA / VS Code (REST Client).
# Start the lesson first: ./mvnw -pl modules/15-observability/lesson spring-boot:run   (starts Grafana LGTM)
# Grafana: http://localhost:3000 (Explore → Tempo for traces, Prometheus for metrics)

### Place an order: creates metrics, a trace over two HTTP hops and JSON log lines with the trace id
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders?isbn=9780134685991&channel=web

### The same via another channel (a counter tag)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders?isbn=9780321336781&channel=app

### Health with the custom warehouse indicator
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### Kubernetes probes
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health/readiness

### All metric names
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics

### One metric, filtered by a tag
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/bookstore.orders.placed?tag=channel:web

### The @Observed timer
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/bookstore.pricing

### Not exposed on purpose (404)
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/env
